    "cornice_return": {
      "group": "massing-and-roof",
      "binding": "forbidden",
      "rule": "No cornice return: the mansard is continuous on every elevation of the mass it crowns, so there is no gable end for a return to stand on.",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "judgment": false,
      "note": "BOUND 30 Sep 2026 (WP-16.2), on Lucas's answer A4 of 30 Sep 2026, recorded in oq/an-inherited-ban-decides-what-the-elevation-may-draw (WP-16.2 stage 2): each of the Italianate family binds its own cornice return forbidden, on its own roof. Until then it was forbidden by GOTHIC-REVIVAL-AMERICAN, on 'The rake is finished in bargeboard, not a boxed classical cornice with mitred returns; a cornice return signals Greek Revival millwork, not Gothic Revival (see distinguished_from).' -- a bargeboarded rake, which is not this style's. This style's own roof leaves a return nowhere to stand: c01 reads 'The mansard shall be continuous on all elevations of the mass it crowns, including rear and side elevations.'"
    },
